  "details": "# Issue:\n\nThis one is a bit complicated to understand, but basically it comes down to this: When you open the Quick Menu User Profile of someone in your instance, the buttons etc listed in the User Profile of everyone else (including your self) will now be the same as the ones you had available for you first opened the profile of.\n\nYou can even open your own profile first and basically remove every button from everyone else, or give your own profile all the normal buttons and send your self a friend request. xD\n\n**Reproduction Steps:**\n\n1. Launch VRChat and open the Main Menu Social Tab\n\n2. Find an instance with others in it and join it\n\n3. Open the Quick Menu Here Tab and click on your profile\n\nIf you do this you will notice that when ever you try to open the Quick Menu User Profile of someone else all the buttons will be missing and their voice slider will have turned into your mic volume slider.\n\nAs I said earlier you can also just click on the profile of someone else and make those buttons stuck.\n\nA few things to note:\n\n- it doesn't matter if you open the profile through the Here Tab or by clicking on the player capsule\n\n- it will stay in this broken state for ever unless you restart your game\n\n- you can for example click on your own profile in your home world, join friends and still have all the buttons missing.\n\n# Expected Behavior:\n\nThe User Profile should switch to the correct state for every user you click on.\n\n# Attachments:\n\nHere is a video showcasing the issue:\n\nhttps://files.catbox.moe/j4pif4.mp4",
